{
    "word": "darbyism",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5def3741-9376-3896-9843-d63b842d8340",
                "word": "Darbyism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6a9ca6bf-3830-375a-9c0f-86976b33f1c4",
                        "entry_id": "5def3741-9376-3896-9843-d63b842d8340",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Christian doctrine formed by John Nelson Darby (1800-1892) and followed by the Exclusive Brethren, which includes a two-stage return of Christ, pretribulation rapture, and seven time periods, called dispensations."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2da59486-b3f8-4afe-a09d-84f935a08bbe",
                                "sense_id": "6a9ca6bf-3830-375a-9c0f-86976b33f1c4",
                                "text": "While however powerless for good, we regret to say it is not so for evil. Although feeble and emasculate, as a Church, to do any service to the cause of the Gospel, Darbyism can, in a certain degree, damage and hinder the Churches that do."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c36aba4b-3216-49ee-b893-997461872922",
                                "sense_id": "6a9ca6bf-3830-375a-9c0f-86976b33f1c4",
                                "text": "Those who discern the signs of the times, will not be slow to perceive that Darbyism is but another form of the high-church ritualistic movement of the day, rising among those called “brethren,” which, though less gross and less outward than much which bears that name elsewhere, is not the less real."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33c1057e-c83a-4dde-8691-1a1dbfb385f8",
                                "sense_id": "6a9ca6bf-3830-375a-9c0f-86976b33f1c4",
                                "text": "The effect of Darbyism upon family life is perhaps its most awful feature."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21c52300-4eb9-4c5e-8922-7aec4c30979f",
                                "sense_id": "6a9ca6bf-3830-375a-9c0f-86976b33f1c4",
                                "text": "One of the major strains of American conservatism that has laid claim to one of the two major political parties in the United States is a theological and political ideology known as Darbyism (dispensationalism)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
